# Netie operating system (DMS)

Generated by `D:\Netie\scripts\netie_init.py`. Do not hand-edit - re-run the script.

## Resume from cold

| # | Source | What it gives you |
|---|--------|-------------------|
| 1 | `CLAUDE.md` in this repo | the invariants you must not break |
| 2 | `D:\Netie\Software Blueprint\DMS\` | the PRD, the epic waves, and the feedback ledger |
| 3 | `gh issue list` in this repo | the live tickets - GitHub is the source of truth, never a markdown backlog |
| 4 | `STATUS.md` | what is true right now (max 60 lines) |

The **feedback ledger** is the PRD's memory: a table mapping every piece of feedback to
the epic it belongs to. It lives with the PRD, not in this repo.

## The routing rule

**Any feature request or defect report you are told about is routed to the PRD Agent
before it is implemented.** Not filed as a ticket. Not built. It decides whether this
belongs to an open epic, a closed one that must reopen, or is a PRD amendment needing the
founder.

An agent that implements unrouted requests is how a PRD and a codebase drift apart, and
the drift stays invisible until a release.

## Agent chain

PRD Agent (slice + feedback intake) -> EPIC Agent (tickets + completeness check) ->
Ticket Runner (execute). Spec: `D:\Netie\Internal\Agents\AGENT_SYSTEM.md`.

**Model policy.** The agent you are talking to runs on whatever model is selected - these
rules do not override it. Only subagent fan-out is pinned: in Cursor use **Grok 4.5 high**
for hard work or **Composer 2.5** for routine.

## File law - five files per repo, no sixth

`CLAUDE.md` (law) - `docs/ACTIVE.md` (map) - `STATUS.md` (state, <=60 lines) -
`CHANGELOG.md` (history, append-only) - `PARKING_LOT.md` (deferred, every entry carries an
unlock condition). Decisions go in `docs/decisions/DR-NNNN-*.md`.

No per-agent files. No per-session files - the answer to "what filename do I store this
session in" is: none, update `STATUS.md`. No dates in filenames outside an archive. IDs
are never reused. Full law: `D:\Netie\Internal\Rules\DOCUMENT_SYSTEM.md`.

## Before deleting anything

Grep the basename across **all** repos and check `git ls-files --error-unmatch`. An
untracked file is not recoverable, and "no production callers" is not "no callers" - a
prior cleanup nearly removed a module three test files imported.
